nce\":\"Inspected /workspace: only task.json exists; task.json says only 'documents.track.md', which is not present; no QuaRot code, no Phi-3 weights, no data, no scripts; pip-imports of torch/transformers/datasets/lm_eval all fail; nproc=24; no GPU accessible; network disabled. Searches for 'quarot', 'phi-3', 'hadamard', 'track.md' across /workspace /tmp /root: zero matches. Topic notes neurips2024/94328/9:setup_1,3,4,6,8,11 named in metadata but not materialized anywhere in the visible filesystem and therefore not observable in this environment.\",\"assumptions\":\"Decision not pinned by topic notes, listed for ruling: (1) Random Hadamard trial count K: proposed seeded K=1 for headline, K=3 for rotation ablation, vs. paper default K=50. (2) GPTQ group size: per-channel locked for headline; group=128 as A2 ablation. (3) Calibration set size: 128x2048 WikiText-2 sequences. (4) Activation precision pairing: headline W{n}A16 with a supplementary W{n}A{n} sub-grid. (5) KV cache: FP16 by default; QuaRot-KV is an explicit ablation. (6) Zero-shot suite: PIQA, WinoGrande, HellaSwag, ARC-E, ARC-C, BoolQ, OBQA, all 0-shot. (7) MMLU excluded by default; flag to include. (8) n-shot left at 0 for fair RTN/GPTQ comparison. (9) Sequence length 2048 sliding window for PPL. (10) PTB as optional third corpus only. (11) Statistical reporting: point estimates in headline, mean+/-std from K=3 only in A1. (12) Reporting format: (method x bitwidth) tables, Pareto plot, FP16 deltas. The task.json itself is treated as ground truth for the question text; the topic-note IDs are not treated as readable content.\",\"uncertainties\":\"Cannot observe the researcher topic notes (neurips2024/94328/9:setup_1,3,4,6,8,11) — present only as metadata IDs, no payload in /workspace. Will need explicit confirmation that the defaults above are acceptable; phantom defaults are not enacted. Cannot verify from this environment whether Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct uses any rope_scaling at runtime (config file not av